Consequences of bad data
Incorrect IC Reconciliation due to errors interpretation of reconciling item leading to not accurate representation of the balance in company ledger
Audit Issues
-Auditors may flag discrepancies or require extensive corrections, leading to delays and increased audit costs.
-In severe cases, it can result in qualified audit opinions or restatements.
Regulatory Non-Compliance
-Errors in tax codes, revenue recognition, or expense classification can lead to violations of accounting standards (e.g., GAAP, IFRS) or tax regulations.
-This may result in fines, penalties, or legal action.
Financial Misstatements
-Incorrect or incomplete data can lead to inaccurate financial statements, which misrepresent the company’s financial health.
Poor Business Decisions
-Inaccurate data leads to misleading KPIs and dashboards, which can cause poor strategic decisions (e.g., overestimating cash flow or profitability).
System Integration Failures
-Bad data can break automated workflows or cause integration errors between ERP, CRM, and reporting systems.


